<para>Unique edge ID number.</para><para>Edges within a graph are numbered consecutively starting at zero, and this method returns the edge&apos;s ID number. ID numbers are unrelated to the order in which edges are inserted, although in the absense of edge erasure they will be assigned consecutively. <ref refid="classSawyer_1_1Container_1_1Graph_1_1Edge" kindref="compound">Edge</ref> ID numbers are stable over insertion of vertices and edges and the erasure of vertices (provided no incident edges are erase), but are not stable over edge erasure. In order to obtain constant-time edge erasure, after an edge is erased the largest-ID edge is renumbered to fill the gap.</para><para><ref refid="classSawyer_1_1Time" kindref="compound">Time</ref> complexity is constant. </para>        </detaileddescription>
